## The Windows credential is in Windows Credential Manager, which a temp USERPROFILE does not change:
PS> cmdkey /list | Select-String Target | Select-String 'antigrav|gemini'
    Destino: LegacyGeneric:target=gemini:antigravity
    Destino: LegacyGeneric:target=gemini-cli-api-key/default-api-key
## The target is fixed (service "gemini", user "antigravity"); no variable or flag of agy 1.5.6
## moves it (strings of agy.exe: no keyring env var; `shouldBypassKeyring` is Linux D-Bus only).
## The Windows logged-out state is therefore not reachable without the operator's /logout.

## Windows: the same isolation with the hidden flag --gemini_dir=<abs tmp>
$ agy --gemini_dir=C:\...\Temp\agyprobe\gd models
exit=0  (13 ids; cli.log: "CLI app data directory: ...\agyprobe\gd\antigravity-cli",
         "ChainedAuth: authenticated via keyring (effective: keyring)")

